            "description": "",
            "summary": "Scholastic Corp. (NASDAQ:SCHL) shares fell after the company reported a wider fiscal 2026 first-quarter loss and results that missed Wall Street expectations on revenue and earnings. Adjusted loss per share was $2.52, missing the consensus estimate of $2.44, while sales of $225.6 million came in below expectations of $238.91 million. Revenue declined 5% from $237.2 million a year ago, pressured by weaker Education Solutions sales in a volatile funding environment. GAAP net loss widened to $71.1",
